# The game's Mac set up once, at build time (BASILISK.RUN): QuickTime 2.5
# installed from the disc with Apple's Installer, and an alias of the game made
# on the desktop for BASILISK.STARTUP to move into Startup Items.
# Click and screen positions are on the Mac's 640x480 screen, in its window.

# The Finder's desktop is up; a click on it gives the Mac the keyboard, and
# with every window closed, typing selects on the desktop.
wait-for 180 Trash
wait 3
click 450 420
key cmd+option+w
wait 2

# Ingenious CD ▸ Quicktime 2.5 Installer ▸ QuickTime™ Install Disk 1 ▸ Install QuickTime™
type Ingenious CD
key cmd+down
wait-for 60 Quicktime 2.5 Installer
type Quicktime 2
key cmd+down
wait-for 60 Install Disk 1
type QuickTime
key cmd+down
wait 4
type Install Q
key cmd+o

# Apple's Installer: Continue, the licence's Agree (it has no default button),
# Install (Easy Install), then Restart.
wait-for 120 Welcome to QuickTime
wait 2
key return
wait-for 60 Disagree
wait 2
# A busy Mac can lose the click, so Agree is clicked until the licence goes.
click-until-gone 60 440 418 Disagree
wait-for 60 Easy Install
wait 2
key return
wait-for 600 Installation was successful
wait 2
key return
# The Mac restarts.
wait-restart 180

# The alias, made in the Finder once the Mac is back: the CD is locked, so the
# Finder offers to make it on the desktop.
wait-for 180 Trash
wait 5
click 450 420
key cmd+option+w
wait 2
type Ingenious CD
key cmd+down
wait-for 60 Quicktime 2.5 Installer
type Ingenious
key cmd+m
wait-for 60 locked
wait 1
key return
wait 3
